PATCH 626: retain the intro script's original sound register lanes (board:0003).

FIST.DAT e61e/e626 loads AL (sound), AH (channel) and DL (normalization)
from ES:cur+2/+3/+4. e62a loads BX from byte cur+5; e62f reads the full
ECX DWORD at DS:(f772+BX). The script byte is a pitch-table BYTE OFFSET,
not pitch and not the complete sound command. e2c2's TCB inbox preserves
EBX independently. The previous generated call dropped all AX/ECX/DL lanes.

Publish the consumed lanes before the existing poster enters the PM gate.
One shared platform owner retains their original widths across native/WASM;
its read-only trace records the actual gate, not a simulated audio stream.
Reuse one source-backed script decoder and one e684/e6a5 stop sequence for
both translated entries into the same original loop. Correct the alternative
entry's script base and six-byte cursor advance at that shared boundary.

The complete matched original 30000-ms trace records all 43 calls to 786a:
40 script commands and stop AX=82ff/81ff/80ff, ECX=0, DL=0. With read-only lane capture on the unchanged parent engine, complete production
runs reach 43 gates on both targets but carry zero lanes. The regression
replays every original packet through the actual patched decoder and checks
full ordered production logs against the independent original trace.

Scope is these consumed intro lanes only. Other mission/damage/weapon
posters, the TCB inbox's full EBX, other control-loop paths, original register
returns/flags, device initialization, DMA/IRQ clock and final mixed PCM remain
open. This does not install a sound producer, force a device active or fit a delay.
